00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.430
In the class, we take three heart rates.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.500
First is a resting heart rate in the beginning of the class.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.490
Next is an active heart rate in the middle of the class.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.990
And last is the recovery heart rate at the end of the class.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.100
Right now, we'd like you to take a resting heart rate.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.340
Find your pulse at your wrist or at your neck.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.930
Two fingers pressed lightly into one side of the neck.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.720
will find that pulse for you.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.500
This is a six second count.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.250
When I say count, count the number of beats.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.720
When I say stop, remember that number.

00:00:40.990 --> 00:00:48.070
Count, stop.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:50.650
Now multiply that number by 10.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.050
60, 70, or 80 beats per minute

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.010
are about average for a resting heart rate.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.420
